    "clock_identity": "The clock projects from the central bay of the southern roof. The same oblique shows the courtyard and north cross-wing behind it and a separate U-plan classroom at left. Its source geometry is a single rectangular area with no inner ring or separate tower primitive.",
    "limits": "Orthophoto eaves and apparent clock-roof midline are measured above ground. The two dates give source accuracy 8.47 m and show different parallax, seasonal tree cover and resampling; historic aerial control establishes the identity and side of the clock, not the ground elevation or detailed tower sides. Southern and northern cross-roofs survive in both images. The absolute roof-to-ground displacement cannot be inferred solely from either image.",
    "model_scope": "A frontage or partial courtyard study must retain the city owner. A possible complete replacement would need intact north and side wings, verified roof/ground clearance and the actual near and distant owner mesh."
  }
